2. Tiny synthetic forward of the encoder and factory (CPU).
3. Real-data readback: heading decisions for the four rooms (inspected, logged); `HeadingFrameDataset` k = 0 / k = 128 checks on the hallway cache.
4. GPU smokes (GPU 0, co-tenant with the peer's evaluation chain, ≤ 3 GB, ≤ 8 CPU threads, never 03:00–04:30 Sep 15, never GPU 1 — peer session's rules), exact commands, each printing `torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated()` at exit: all run through `tools/exp06_smoke.py --entry <name> -- <argv>` (same-process peak-memory report, 300 s alarm, `diagnostic` receipt): (a) trainer parity: entries `trainer` and `exp06_train`, both with `--backbone simple --save-dir ckpt/exp06/_smoke/t0 --epochs 1 --max-train-batches 3 --max-test-batches 2 --batch-size 4 --num-workers 4 --save-every 0 --no-save` (TF32 off) → identical printed losses; (b) entry `exp06_train` with `--backbone cylindrical_oriented --save-dir ckpt/exp06/_smoke/t1 --epochs 1 --max-train-batches 3 --max-test-batches 2 --batch-size 4 --num-workers 4 --save-every 0 --no-save`; (c) fixture: `python tools/exp06_smoke.py --make-fixture ckpt/exp06/_smoke/fixture_cylor.pth`; HAA stage-1 smoke: entry `exp06_haa_finetune` with `--backbone cylindrical_oriented --init ckpt/exp06/_smoke/fixture_cylor.pth --rooms class_room --heading-json-dir ckpt/exp06/heading --save-dir ckpt/exp06/_smoke/h1 --epochs 2 --val-every 1 --batch-size 4 --val-batch-size 4`; (d) HAA eval smoke: entry `exp06_haa_eval` with `--backbone cylindrical_oriented --checkpoint ckpt/exp06/_smoke/h1/best.pth --heading-json-dir ckpt/exp06/heading --rooms hallway --max-samples 4 --save-dir ckpt/exp06/_smoke/e1`; `ckpt/exp06/_smoke/` is deleted afterwards. The runner aborts and reports any smoke exceeding 3 GB or 300 s.
5. **Bounded fit/timing probe** on the target card when it is free: 200 batches at the full 32 × 2 recipe, `--no-save`, peak memory and s/iter recorded; full launch only if the extrapolated epoch time ≤ 1.15 × 156 min.
